            0.475,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "PAIR OF LINEAR EQUATIONS IN TWO VARIABLES"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.874,
            0.104,
            0.898,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "37"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.144,
            0.902,
            0.197
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) Meena went to a bank to withdraw ` 2000. She asked the cashier to give her ` 50 and ` 100 notes only. Meena got 25 notes in all. Find how many notes of ` 50 and ` 100 she received."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.203,
            0.902,
            0.276
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(v) A lending library has a fixed charge for the first three days and an additional charge for each day thereafter. Saritha paid ` 27 for a book kept for seven days, while Susy paid ` 21 for the book she kept for five days. Find the fixed charge and the charge for each extra day."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.289,
            0.252,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.4 Summary"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.315,
            0.574,
            0.334
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In this chapter, you have studied the following points:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.339,
            0.857,
            0.357
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A pair of linear equations in two variables can be represented, and solved, by the:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.361,
            0.36,
            0.379
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) graphical method"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.384,
            0.358,
            0.402
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) algebraic method"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.407,
            0.326,
            0.425
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Graphical Method :"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.432,
            0.866,
            0.45
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The graph of a pair of linear equations in two variables is represented by two lines."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.17,
            0.455,
            0.9,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) If the lines intersect at a point, then that point gives the unique solution of the two equations. In this case, the pair of equations is "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "consistent",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.495,
            0.901,
            0.548
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) If the lines coincide, then there are infinitely many solutions — each point on the line being a solution. In this case, the pair of equations is "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "dependent (consistent)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.554,
            0.9,
            0.59
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) If the lines are parallel, then the pair of equations has no solution. In this case, the pair of equations is "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "inconsistent",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.597,
            0.9,
            0.634
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Algebraic Methods : We have discussed the following methods for finding the solution(s) of a pair of linear equations :"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.637,
            0.392,
            0.655
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Substitution Method"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.659,
            0.382,
            0.676
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Elimination Method"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.681,
            0.9,
            0.716
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If a pair of linear equations is given by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a_{1}x + b_{1}y + c_{1} = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a_{2}x + b_{2}y + c_{2} = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , then the following situations can arise :"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.724,
            0.762,
            0.763
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{a_{1}}{a_{2}} \\neq \\frac{b_{1}}{b_{1}}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " : In this case, the pair of linear equations is consistent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.768,
            0.822,
            0.811
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{a_{1}}{a_{2}}=\\frac{b_{1}}{b_{2}}\\neq\\frac{c_{1}}{c_{2}}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " : In this case, the pair of linear equations is inconsistent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.823,
            0.899,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { a _ { 1 } } { a _ { 2 } }   =   \\frac { b _ { 1 } } { b _ { 2 } }   =   \\frac { c _ { 1 } } { c _ { 2 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " : In this case, the pair of linear equations is dependent and consistent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.864,
            0.902,
            0.916
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " There are several situations which can be mathematically represented by two equations that are not linear to start with. But we alter them so that they are reduced to a pair of linear equations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
            0.967,
            0.562,
            0.982
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
